*  RED (s106) -- THE SEMANTIC WITNESS, NO CRASH.  A bare call in an ALT arm of a pattern-valued
*  GOAL-SNOBOL4-100 R-4(b)/eager-call witness set (s106).  Oracle: /home/claude/x64/bin/sbl -b <file>
*  expression must be called AT PATTERN CONSTRUCTION TIME (manual p.86 "captures the value at
*  the time of pattern construction"; p.134 "Without it, PUSH() is called when the pattern is
*  first constructed").  SCRIP defers it into the PAT$ blob and calls it at MATCH time.
*  Oracle: CALLED up / BUILT / MATCHED.   SCRIP: BUILT / CALLED up / MATCHED.
*  Top level, so it does NOT crash -- this is the pure ordering divergence, and it proves the
*  "green" top-level controls beside this file are green ONLY because up() is side-effect free.
        DEFINE('up(up)')                :(up_end)
up      OUTPUT = 'CALLED up'
        up = REPLACE(up, &LCASE, &UCASE)  :(RETURN)
up_end
        c = 'a'
        P = LEN(0)
        P = P (up(c) | c)
        OUTPUT = 'BUILT'
        'A' P                           :F(NO)
        OUTPUT = 'MATCHED'              :(FIN)
NO      OUTPUT = 'NOMATCH'
FIN
END
